# Burden of Proof on Bot2's Novice Inspector (1/2): the Inspector is a Detective but not one Bot1, the Aura's controller, controls, so the +2/+2 stays off
# ("you control" is the Aura's controller, not the creature's) and the "otherwise" half applies: base 1/1, and it can't block Detectives. On turn 3 Bot1
# attacks with its own Novice Inspector and a Memnite: Bot2's enchanted Inspector may not block the Detective, may block the Memnite (both 1/1s die and the Aura goes to the graveyard), and the
# Detective hits for 1.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Novice Inspector
Memnite
Burden of Proof
Island x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Novice Inspector
Island x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Novice Inspector.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Novice Inspector.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Burden of Proof.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Novice Inspector)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot2.Battlefield.Novice Inspector.Power = 1
? Bot2.Battlefield.Novice Inspector.Toughness = 1
Bot1.Attack(Novice Inspector > Bot2; Memnite > Bot2)
! Bot2.Block(Novice Inspector > Novice Inspector)
Bot2.Block(Novice Inspector > Memnite)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 19
Bot2.Graveyard = Novice Inspector
Bot1.Graveyard = Burden of Proof; Memnite
